Located in Klebang, this is the first and only submarine museum in the country. The submarine itself was the SMD Quessant, decommissioned by the French Navy and later used as a training vessel by the Royal Malaysian Navy from 2005 to 2009. It still contains its original equipment such as the torpedo launching platform, torpedo bays, navigational and communications equipment, as well as its engine room. Venture into the past as you board this majestic vessel and explore the interior of spaces such as the crew's living quarters and corridors.
